# Per-Dockerfile ignore override for Dockerfile.ssr (BuildKit picks
# "<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore" over the plain .dockerignore for a build
# using that specific -f). Deliberately keeps only a minimal set of
# exclusions from the real .dockerignore — dist, node_modules, package.json,
# public, vite.config.js, index.html, .env, and the src/dms/packages/dms
# exclusions are all needed by the SSR client+server build and must NOT be
# excluded here. See setup/tasks/current/enable-ssr-mode.md.
#
# .env is deliberately NOT excluded (unlike the real .dockerignore, and
# unlike an earlier version of this file): `npm run build:ssr` runs Vite's
# client build inside this Dockerfile's builder stage via `COPY . .`, and
# Vite bakes VITE_* vars into the compiled client bundle at build time. If
# .env isn't present in the build context, VITE_DMS_APP resolves to
# undefined and App.jsx's `|| "wcdb"` fallback gets compiled in statically —
# real bug hit and fixed 2026-08-27 (the SSR HTML was correct, but
# the client bundle that hydrated it was wired for the wrong site). The
# runtime stage only COPYs specific paths from the builder (dist,
# node_modules, dms-server, dms/src, data-types, entry-ssr.jsx) — .env is
# never copied into the final image, so this doesn't leak secrets there;
# it's only present in the (unpublished, local-only) builder-stage layer.

*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal

.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store

**/ritis.config.json
